{:edb/db-before-t 2792 :edb/db-after-t 2793 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536105 50 #inst "2026-10-09T15:05:01.157Z" 13194139536105 true] [17592186133666 1020 #edb/ref 17592186383851 13194139536105 true] [17592186133666 1020 #edb/ref 17592186383865 13194139536105 true] [17592186133666 1020 #edb/ref 17592186383872 13194139536105 true] [17592186133667 1020 #edb/ref 17592186383858 13194139536105 true] [17592186133667 1020 #edb/ref 17592186383879 13194139536105 true] [17592186383851 1017 #edb/ref 17592186383852 13194139536105 true] [17592186383851 1089 "q-110471" 13194139536105 true] [17592186383851 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536105 true] [17592186383851 1100 "Suppose that the elementary row operation \n${R}_{2}:=3{R}_{2}$ is applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" 13194139536105 true] [17592186383851 1113 #uuid "c63ff4bb-da6b-5999-bbc7-816dc82a29a6" 13194139536105 true] [17592186383851 1145 "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:=3{R}_{2}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" 13194139536105 true] [17592186383852 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383853 13194139536105 true] [17592186383852 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383854 13194139536105 true] [17592186383852 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383855 13194139536105 true] [17592186383852 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383856 13194139536105 true] [17592186383852 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383857 13194139536105 true] [17592186383852 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536105 true] [17592186383852 1041 "selection" 13194139536105 true] [17592186383852 1104 #edb/ref 17592186383857 13194139536105 true] [17592186383852 1110 #uuid "d1c3165d-bd53-5d9a-a729-a417d9b41a88" 13194139536105 true] [17592186383853 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" 13194139536105 true] [17592186383853 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536105 true] [17592186383853 1111 #uuid "76e1d450-b3ef-57af-9c64-ab8be1886d53" 13194139536105 true] [17592186383854 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" 13194139536105 true] [17592186383854 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536105 true] [17592186383854 1111 #uuid "c7229ed6-7988-530d-a977-60c39c21da12" 13194139536105 true] [17592186383855 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" 13194139536105 true] [17592186383855 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536105 true] [17592186383855 1111 #uuid "c74b1327-57a3-5079-9810-08cee14b8c4f" 13194139536105 true] [17592186383856 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" 13194139536105 true] [17592186383856 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536105 true] [17592186383856 1111 #uuid "e8acb90f-f0ff-5180-b4c9-3f2ce56526ea" 13194139536105 true] [17592186383857 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" 13194139536105 true] [17592186383857 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536105 true] [17592186383857 1111 #uuid "4a9a90e1-5dba-5ab0-9ee2-104f8632a37f" 13194139536105 true] [17592186383858 1017 #edb/ref 17592186383859 13194139536105 true] [17592186383858 1089 "q-32133" 13194139536105 true] [17592186383858 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536105 true] [17592186383858 1100 "Suppose that the following elementary row operations are applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ in the given order:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1}\n$$\n\nWhat is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" 13194139536105 true] [17592186383858 1113 #uuid "324f3608-babb-59d3-b059-1a5e8e0a8c0c" 13194139536105 true] [17592186383858 1145 "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" 13194139536105 true] [17592186383859 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383860 13194139536105 true] [17592186383859 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383861 13194139536105 true] [17592186383859 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383862 13194139536105 true] [17592186383859 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383863 13194139536105 true] [17592186383859 1000 #edb/ref 175921863838